course: dictionary
lesson: 2850
title: A word with a story: dodo
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dodo is a bird, but dodo is also a word with more than one meaning. Read the words around it to find which meaning is used. «The dodo was a big flightless pigeon from Mauritius» tells you it is an animal, because it lives on an island and cannot fly.
explain: Dodo can be used in other ways too. «As dead as a dodo» means completely gone or finished, so the clue is the phrase, not the bird. If someone calls you a dodo, they may mean you are old-fashioned or silly.
explain: The word comes from a real animal that is now gone. The dodo lived only on the island of Mauritius and was not afraid of people, because it had no enemies there. That made it easy to hunt.
fact: A dodo is a large, plump bird that could not fly.
fact: The dodo lived only on the island of Mauritius in the Indian Ocean.
fact: «As dead as a dodo» means completely gone or finished.
fact: «Dodo» can also mean an old-fashioned or silly person (informal).
fact: The dodo became extinct after sailors arrived, hunted it, and brought animals that ate its eggs.
exercise: «The dodo was a big flightless pigeon from Mauritius.» What does flightless mean? | Covered in bright feathers | Able to swim far out to sea | Very fast on the ground | *Unable to fly
exercise: Dad says about his old phone, «It is as dead as a dodo.» What does he mean? | Sleeping very deeply | Lost somewhere in the house | Very healthy and full of energy | *Completely finished, no longer working
exercise: «The dodo was not stupid; it had lived with no hunters, so it had no reason to fear people.» Why was the dodo not afraid of people? | *It had lived with no hunters | It was too big to be seen | People fed it every day | It could fly away quickly
test: Tom's grandma says, «Don't be such a dodo, we always used a paper map!» What does dodo mean here? | *An old-fashioned or silly person | A kind of map | A sailor who hunts birds | A large bird from Mauritius
test: «The dodo became extinct after sailors arrived.» What does extinct mean? | Hiding in a cave | *No longer alive anywhere in the world | Very hungry | Brand new and never used
exam: Which sentence uses dodo to mean the bird? | Ella is the dodo of the class, she says. | Don't be such a dodo, Sam. | «As dead as a dodo» is what the sign says. | *«The dodo lived only on the island of Mauritius.»
